---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import Statement from '../components/Statement.astro';
import { plan, money } from '../data/business';
import { organizationSchema } from '../data/schema';

const title = 'Noven — Get found when customers ask AI who to use';
const description =
  'Noven helps accountants, solicitors, clinics, consultancies and agencies get found and recommended when customers ask ChatGPT, Google, Copilot or Perplexity who to use. Start with a £30 audit.';

const audit = plan('audit');
const foundation = plan('foundation');
const maintain = plan('maintain');

// Not a copy of the structured data — the structured data. The layout renders
// this exact object into the page head.
const orgSchema = organizationSchema(Astro.site);
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <h1>When your customers ask an AI who to use, the answer should include you.</h1>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal>
          People increasingly ask ChatGPT, Google, Copilot and Perplexity to recommend an
          accountant, a solicitor, a clinic or a consultancy — instead of scrolling through search
          results. Noven does the work that gets your business into those answers.
        </p>
        <div data-reveal>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/contact/">
              Book the {money(audit.price)} audit
              <svg width="14" height="10" viewBox="0 0 14 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path
                  d="M9 1l4 4-4 4M13 5H1"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  stroke-linecap="square"></path>
              </svg>
            </a>
            <a href="/how-it-works/">See how it works</a>
          </div>
          <p class="cta-note">
            A written report on where you currently show up, and what's in the way. No obligation
            beyond the {money(audit.price)}.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal>
        <Code
          caption="What an AI assistant reads on this page"
          label="Noven's structured data, as JSON-LD"
          data={orgSchema}
          note="This is the real thing — the same block sits in this page's source, and it's the part a visitor never sees. Most business websites have nothing here at all."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split split--sticky">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Why does this matter now?</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          Buying habits have changed. Someone who needs a professional service used to type a query
          into Google and compare the results themselves. Now, many of them ask an AI assistant a
          direct question — <em>"Who's a good commercial solicitor near Manchester?"</em> — and get
          a short list of named businesses back.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your business isn't in that short list, you're not losing a ranking position. You're
          simply not part of the conversation, and you won't know it's happening, because there's
          no results page to check.
        </p>
        <p>
          The businesses that do appear are the ones whose information the AI systems can find,
          read and trust. That is fixable, and it's what Noven does.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div data-reveal>
          <h2>What does Noven actually do?</h2>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal>
          <p>
            Noven makes your business easy for AI assistants to find, understand and recommend. In
            practice that means three kinds of work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stages">
        <div class="stage" data-reveal>
          <div class="stage-head">
            <h3>We find out where you stand.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-body">
            <p>
              We ask the major AI assistants the questions your customers ask, record what they say
              about you and your competitors, and trace why.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage" data-reveal>
          <div class="stage-head">
            <h3>We fix what's blocking you.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-body">
            <p>
              Most businesses are invisible to these systems for mundane, correctable reasons:
              information the crawlers can't read, inconsistent facts across the web, or pages that
              never answer the questions customers actually ask.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage" data-reveal>
          <div class="stage-head">
            <h3>We keep you visible.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-body">
            <p>
              The assistants and their sources change constantly. Ongoing plans keep your
              information current and extend your coverage to more of the questions that matter to
              you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Statement
        cite="There is no button we press that makes an AI recommend you. There is a set of things these systems demonstrably rely on, and we make sure you have them."
      >
        It's methodical work, <em>not a trick.</em>
      </Statement>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split split--sticky">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Who is this for?</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          Service businesses whose customers research and compare before buying: accountants,
          solicitors, private clinics, consultancies and agencies. If a client is worth hundreds or
          thousands of pounds to you, being one of the three names an AI suggests is worth taking
          seriously.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's a poor fit if your customers buy on impulse, or if you already have more work than
          you can take on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--invert">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Where's the proof?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div data-reveal>
          <p>
            Noven is a new business, and we don't yet have client case studies to show you. We won't
            invent any, and we'd encourage you to be suspicious of anyone in this field who shows
            you numbers that can't be checked.
          </p>
          <p>
            What we can show you is this website. It's built exactly the way we build for clients —
            plain, fast pages that assistants can read, structured information about the business,
            and a <a href="/faq/">real FAQ</a> that answers the questions people actually ask. Try
            it yourself: ask ChatGPT or Perplexity what Noven does and how much it costs, and see
            what comes back.
          </p>
          <p class="flag">
            [PLACEHOLDER: client case studies will be published here, with permission, as the first
            engagements complete.]
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split split--sticky">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>What does it cost?</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          One service, priced in plain numbers. It starts with a
          <strong>{money(audit.price)} audit</strong> of where you currently show up. If there's
          work worth doing, the <strong>{money(foundation.price)} Foundation</strong> setup gets you
          visible, and a monthly plan from <strong>{money(maintain.price)}</strong> keeps you that
          way. Full details, including what's in each part, are on the
          <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The audit is deliberately cheap so that finding out where you stand is an easy decision.
          If the audit shows you're already in good shape, we'll say so, and that's the end of it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
